AB  - The rapid advancement of IoT-driven healthcare monitoring has enabled real-time disease prediction and patient management. HealthSenseFusion is an integrated AI model that leverages edge computing, federated learning, and deep learning to enhance remote healthcare monitoring and anomaly detection. The model was evaluated across multiple health conditions, achieving an accuracy of 94.2% for cardiovascular disease detection, 92.8% for respiratory disorders, 91.5% for diabetes monitoring, and 96.1% for general anomaly detection. By integrating Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) and Bidirectional Long Short-Term Memory (Bi-LSTM) with an attention mechanism, HealthSenseFusion significantly improves prediction accuracy, inference speed, and computational efficiency. In comparison with existing models, HealthSenseFusion reduced inference time by 50% and improved privacy compliance with federated learning and homomorphic encryption. The real-time anomaly detection module demonstrated 96.5% accuracy in identifying sudden heart rate drops and 97.1% accuracy in detecting abnormal Sp02 fluctuations. Additionally, early intervention using this system reduced mortality rates by up to 54.5% in diabetic complications and 48.4% in cardiac arrest cases. With its optimized energy efficiency (10W power consumption) and low-cost processing ($1.00 per 1000 predictions), HealthSenseFusion presents a scalable, secure, and highly accurate healthcare monitoring solution for real-world deployment.
ER  - 

