AB  - Cancer is one of the most commonly diagnosed health issue in these days. To detect cancer at an early stage and classify accurately, we train a model on a large dataset of 26 cancer types. In this manuscript, we introduce a multi-class cancer classification framework using Horizontal Federated Learning (HFL) for sustainable healthcare. It provides multiple clients to jointly train a multi-class cancer classification model without sharing any personal information. We incorporate Homomorphic Encryption (HE) before sharing weights with the global model. This process improves patient privacy and data security. We used four ImageNet-based models in our experiments: MobileNetV2, ResNet50, ResNet18, and EfficientNet_B0. We trained these models in a centralized setting and achieved the best accuracy with EfficientNet_B0 at 98.72%. We conducted 5 rounds of experiments in HFL setting, with and without HE, to evaluate accuracy. The highest global model test accuracy is 99.72% without HE, using MobileNetV2, and 99.78% with HE, using ResNet50. These results demonstrate that the proposed framework performs well and can classify all cancer types.
ER  - 

