AB  - The fast development of the Internet of Medical Things (IoMT) has greatly revolutionized contemporary healthcare by allowing real-time patient monitoring, diagnosis, and treatment due to the interconnecting medical devices and smart sensors. Nevertheless, the issue of privacy, security, and scalability of patient data is crucially important when considering healthcare data analysis through the conventional centralized machine learning methods because of the necessity to transfer To overcome these issues, the paper introduces a proposal of a Secure and Scalable Federated Learning Framework of Healthcare IoMT (SSFL-HIoMT) that allows multiple medical tools and healthcare organizations to collaboratively train machine learning models without exchanging raw patient data. Within the suggested scheme, federated learning would enable local IoMT devices to train models using their local datasets and transfer encrypted model updates to a central server, thus maintaining the confidentiality of patients. In order to improve even more securities and privacy protection, the framework incorporates homomorphic encryption and differentially privacy to ensure that the update to the model and avoids data leakage when performing the aggregation process. Also, a verification layer is integrated through a blockchain-based platform to guarantee transparency, traceability, and trust between involved healthcare parties by storing transactions of model updates through a secure system. The edge and fog computing architectures are also used in the framework to enhance scalability, minimize the communication overhead, and facilitate efficient computations in heterogeneous IoMT settings. Experimental analyses reveal that the proposed SSFL-HIoMT framework has a superior model accuracy, better privacy protection, lower communication cost and greater security attack resistance than the current federated learning frameworks, including FEEL, FedCure and FedCare. Thus, the presented solution is an effective and trustworthy way to ensure privacy-saving collaborative healthcare analytics and contribute to the creation of safe and smart IoMT-based healthcare systems.
ER  - 

